    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Enrich company websites in Google Sheets with contact emails, phones and socials using Weio\n\n### Who it's for\nSales teams, agencies and founders who keep a list of prospect or customer companies in Google Sheets and want the public contact details from each company's website filled in next to it, instead of copying them by hand.\n\n### How it works\n1. Runs every day at 7:00 (or on demand) and reads your sheet.\n2. Keeps the rows that have a `website` and were never enriched, or were enriched more than 90 days ago. Each website is looked up once per run, at most 100 per run (both numbers are in **Settings**).\n3. For each website it calls the Weio site-info API, which reads the company's homepage and returns what the business publishes about itself: page title and description, CMS or site builder, whether the page has a mobile viewport tag, role email addresses (info@, sales@, office@...; personal-name addresses are left out on purpose), phone numbers, social profile links and the contact or about page. It also flags a broken HTTPS certificate.\n4. Writes the results back to the same row, matched on `website`. A site with contact details gets every column; a site without them gets its status and site facts; an unreachable or invalid address gets its status only. A re-check therefore never erases contact details you already have.\n5. Pauses between lookups, then emails one summary: how many rows got contact details, which ones, and how many credits are left on your key.\n6. If the API key is missing, invalid or out of credits, the run stops at once instead of marking every row as failed, and the **Error Trigger** branch emails you the reason.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a sheet with a header row: `website`, `enrich_status`, `enriched_at`, `site_title`, `site_description`, `cms`, `mobile_friendly`, `emails`, `phones`, `contact_page`, `linkedin`, `facebook`, `instagram`, `other_socials`. Only `website` is required; columns you leave out are skipped.\n2. Get a Weio API key, then create an n8n **Header Auth** credential named `Weio API key` with Name `Authorization` and Value `Bearer wk_...` (your key). Select it on **Look up website facts**.\n3. In **Settings**, paste your sheet URL and tab name and set your email address.\n4. Select your Google Sheets credential on **Read leads** and the three **Save** nodes, and your Gmail credential on both email nodes. Put your address in **Email: workflow failed** as well.\n5. In the workflow settings, choose this workflow as its own error workflow. Run it once on a few rows, then activate it.\n\n### Requirements\n- A Weio API key: $9 for 1,000 lookups, valid for 12 months, emailed automatically after Stripe checkout: [weio.ai site check API](https://weio.ai/services/site-check-api.html?utm_source=n8n&utm_medium=templates&utm_campaign=site-enrich). This endpoint has no free tier. Every lookup uses one credit, including websites that turn out to be unreachable; invalid addresses, rate-limit and \"busy\" answers are not charged.\n- Google Sheets and Gmail accounts. Only core n8n nodes are used.\n\n### Customization\nChange the schedule, the re-check window, the per-run cap or the pause in **Settings**. Swap Gmail for Slack or Outlook, or write to Airtable or your CRM instead of Google Sheets.\n\n### Good to know\nAll data comes from each business's own public homepage (one page per lookup), so sites that list contacts only on other pages return fewer details. Role addresses are still business contact data: follow privacy and anti-spam law (for example CAN-SPAM, GDPR or CASL) when you contact anyone.\n\nMade by Weio, Inc. (Santa Barbara, CA). This template was built by Weio's AI operators.",
        "height": 1560,
        "width": 680
      },
